{
 "name": "Inbox · Send",
 "nodes": [
  {
   "parameters": {
    "content": "## Inbox · Send (Lesson 5.7)\nOne sender for every reply and note: { conversation_id, channel, thread_id, text, reply_to_message_id, last_customer_msg_at, sent_by }.\nChannel rules in code first: email always; WhatsApp, Instagram and Messenger free-form only within 24 hours of the customer's last message (outside it: an approved template, or Tolu decides).\nEvery message sent is logged in messages.\n\nCredentials: Gmail (support inbox); WhatsApp API; Header Auth \"Meta page token\" (Authorization: Bearer + Page token); Postgres; Telegram.\nPlaceholders: YOUR_PHONE_NUMBER_ID, YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID.",
    "height": 320,
    "width": 540
   },
   "id": "69e3f50e-cda9-4a90-b43f-7064541086a7",
   "name": "Note 1",
   "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
   "typeVersion": 1,
   "position": [
    -600,
    -340
   ]
  },
  {
   "parameters": {},
   "id": "7024dc52-8611-4f45-bbaa-fad9ddfc82ed",
   "name": "When called",
   "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
   "typeVersion": 1,
   "position": [
    0,
    0
   ]
  },
  {
   "parameters": {
    "jsCode": "const h = (Date.now() - new Date($json.last_customer_msg_at)) / 36e5;\nconst allowed = $json.channel === 'email' || h <= 24;\nreturn { ...$json, allowed, reason: allowed ? '' : `${$json.channel}: more than 24 hours since the customer's last message` };\n",
    "mode": "runOnceForEachItem"
   },
